*Eager execution* means an operation runs immediately instead of waiting for later enumeration. <xref:System.Linq.Enumerable.ToList*> executes the query immediately and stores its results in a list. Both passes now read the stored attendees without running the sort again. In contrast, defining the `OrderBy` query still defers the sort: it reads and buffers all input only when enumeration begins. Buffering doesn't mean the query executes when you define it. Use a snapshot when you need to reuse results without recalculating them; keep the deferred query when you want each enumeration to read the current input. See Compose queries with cached results.

